1
00:00:01,180 --> 00:00:03,440
We are team Minus Zero:

2
00:00:03,440 --> 00:00:08,100
Ahmad Farruk Towsif and MD Toslim Uddin Rahat.

3
00:00:08,100 --> 00:00:10,940
Our project is Mission Architect,

4
00:00:10,940 --> 00:00:14,310
built for the Space Mission Design Game challenge.

5
00:00:15,060 --> 00:00:19,110
Real space missions take years and huge teams

6
00:00:19,110 --> 00:00:22,430
to design, so students never get to feel

7
00:00:22,430 --> 00:00:25,100
how mission design actually works —

8
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:27,720
how one choice about fuel,

9
00:00:27,720 --> 00:00:32,960
power or money decides whether a mission lives or dies.

10
00:00:33,940 --> 00:00:37,490
Mission Architect turns that into a game anyone

11
00:00:37,490 --> 00:00:39,050
can play in a browser.

12
00:00:40,110 --> 00:00:41,570
You pick a destination —

13
00:00:41,570 --> 00:00:43,290
the Moon, Mars,

14
00:00:43,290 --> 00:00:45,750
or asteroid Bennu —

15
00:00:45,750 --> 00:00:48,970
choose a real rocket and engine,

16
00:00:48,970 --> 00:00:52,670
and build your spacecraft part by part.

17
00:00:53,800 --> 00:00:57,380
A real rocket equation checks your delta-v live.

18
00:00:58,510 --> 00:01:00,970
Too heavy, no power,

19
00:01:00,970 --> 00:01:02,570
not enough fuel —

20
00:01:02,570 --> 00:01:05,860
the game will not let you launch,

21
00:01:05,860 --> 00:01:09,030
and it tells you why in plain language.

22
00:01:09,920 --> 00:01:13,700
In flight, real dangers strike:

23
00:01:13,700 --> 00:01:17,380
solar flares, dust storms,

24
00:01:17,380 --> 00:01:21,250
equipment failures. Whether you survive depends

25
00:01:21,250 --> 00:01:22,740
on what you built.

26
00:01:23,700 --> 00:01:27,300
Every mission ends with a grade and a

27
00:01:27,300 --> 00:01:30,710
debrief that explains your own decisions.

28
00:01:31,830 --> 00:01:33,640
It runs in any browser,

29
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:37,010
on a phone or a computer,

30
00:01:37,010 --> 00:01:38,770
by mouse or keyboard.

31
00:01:40,080 --> 00:01:44,620
Our game runs on real NASA data:

32
00:01:44,620 --> 00:01:47,450
the NASA Open Science Data Repository,

33
00:01:47,450 --> 00:01:49,800
including radiation data;

34
00:01:49,800 --> 00:01:53,450
NASA Planetary Fact Sheets for distance,

35
00:01:53,450 --> 00:01:55,260
gravity and delta-v;

36
00:01:55,260 --> 00:01:59,660
the NASA JPL Small-Body Database for asteroid Bennu;

37
00:01:59,660 --> 00:02:05,400
and NASA DONKI space-weather data behind our solar flare events.

38
00:02:06,360 --> 00:02:08,440
Mission Architect — design it,

39
00:02:08,440 --> 00:02:09,790
build it, fly it.

40
00:02:09,790 --> 00:02:11,240
Play it live —

41
00:02:11,240 --> 00:02:13,640
the link is on our project page.

